WEBVTT

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.820
I have this vague memory.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.200
I saw you ages ago, or rather, Pope did.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.540
Kagero, who or what are you?

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:24.340
And what is this building?
It's not just some hideout.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.050
You're a sharp one, Arashi.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.220
Actually, this is what we call an Ark.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.720
In other words, a spaceship.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.550
A spaceship?

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.100
This is the one I arrived on

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:42.100
2,000 years ago as part of the
immigrant group from the Moon.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.740
The Kunad Gate is stable.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:33.250
A 2,000-Year Ambition

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.050
Wh-What are you
talking about, Kagero?

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.760
You came from the moon?

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.800
As one of the immigrants?

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.970
Don't be stupid.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:41.100
That would mean you were
born over 2,000 years ago!

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.850
Yep! I may not look it, but I'm
an old man, so show some respect.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.350
Would you cut the crap already?!

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:51.820
Kyoka, Arashi. I take it
you know what this is.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.200
Wait, are those...?

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.950
Cold sleep capsules.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.910
Cold sleep?

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:04.080
Are you sure about that, you two?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.330
Yes.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.830
But it's supposed to still be theoretical.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.920
Something's been bothering me
ever since we got here.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.840
Not only this place, but also
the buildings. They're not normal.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.640
The whole spaceship thing
doesn't seem that far-fetched.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.100
So then it's all true?

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.850
If so, then there are other
immigrants like you?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:29.270
The people you see in Togetsu are
Design Children for the most part.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:34.820
The remaining immigrants that
yet live are in cold sleep like I was.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.530
I'm not buying it.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.450
Yeah, it does sound crazy at first.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.700
However, it's all true.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.250
You're really over 2,000 years old?

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:52.500
I knew your ancestor, Yakumo Sumeragi,
founding father of New Himuka quite well.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.630
Huh?

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.380
Guys, you have company!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.300
Togetsu! They found us!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.390
No! They're...

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.810
OSF?! From Suoh?!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.790
Kagero!

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.200
Tsugumi?

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:30.670
Hanabi!

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.750
I'm with you!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:33.750
Kyoka!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.000
Okay!

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:39.840
Everyone all right?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.010
Yeah, I'm with Kyoka.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.350
I'm with Luka. What about Tsugumi?

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.890
I'm with Kagero.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.770
We escaped with Shiden!

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:50.310
Kasane?! Do you read me?!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:53.190
Haruka? Is this telepathy?

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:56.190
Psynet's been hijacked by Suoh.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.990
My brother's looking into countermeasures.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.530
But it's going to take time.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.030
It seems Suoh dispatched a pursuit team.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.200
Be careful.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.870
I want you all back in one piece.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.210
Let's go, Tsugumi.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.800
Okay.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.630
Kasane Randall?

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.550
She's joined forces
with Lieutenant Sumeragi.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.890
They're now on the run on Hieno Mountain.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.930
Our target is the rebel Yuito Sumeragi.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.140
Bring him in at all costs.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.310
Yes, sir!

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.570
I think we lost them.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.440
Yeah.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.150
They're still searching for us.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:50.290
There's a cavern about 5 km
west by southwest of here.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.040
It will take us down to
the base of the mountain.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.420
That whole area is supposed
to be restricted.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.250
Why? Is something there?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.750
I don't know.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.260
It was placed off-limits
long before I was born.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.970
Well, we <i>are </i>taking a risk
if we go that way.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:09.010
But we can't turn back.
They're still after us.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.020
Then we keep moving forward.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:14.190
Yeah, the OSF isn't our true enemy.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.850
I want to avoid a fight.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.730
Okay, see you at the rendezvous point.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:22.070
We should stay in contact via brain talk.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.780
Roger.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.160
Let's go.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:34.210
Kagero.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.830
You said you knew Yakumo Sumeragi.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.000
Is that true?

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.300
It is.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:44.380
He was the leader of our immigrant group.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.550
What?!

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.550
I've heard that story, too.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.640
They say he was a fine leader.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:56.230
He was really cheerful
and unbelievably positive.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.770
Yakumo led the immigrant
group's Ark landings on earth

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.900
and began efforts to improve
the planet's environment

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.700
and pave the way for more immigrants.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:11.200
However, the project was
scrapped before it was complete.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.450
What happened?

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.910
The computer in Togetsu told us

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:19.630
the Extinction Belt appeared after
the immigrant group landed on earth.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:24.590
The immigration project was halted
after the belt appeared?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:27.680
I heard it was because the situation
on the Moon changed.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.300
Something had come from space or...

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.470
Kyoka, even you are
completely in the dark?

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:40.560
All right, this may take a while,
but here's what happened 2,000 years ago.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.360
After we landed on earth,
we remained in contact with the Moon.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.740
That's when we learned
something had gone wrong.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:54.580
A disease that turned humans into monsters
started spreading on the Moon.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:56.080
Did you say monsters?!

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.410
You mean...!

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.790
That's right, the Others.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:04.710
A comet had passed near the Moon.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:10.010
It left behind an unknown substance
that rained down.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:16.810
All life that came in contact with
the substance was transformed into Others.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:21.350
The Moon's government named
the substance Other Particles.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:26.860
Meanwhile, the earth redevelopment effort
entered the gravity control phase.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.700
The Moon's government
believed it could prevent

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.620
the Other Particles
from falling to the Moon.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:33.870
Don't tell me...

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:40.120
That's right. They launched a project
to divert the Other Particles to earth.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.670
That's the origin of the Extinction Belt.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:44.590
But...

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:49.550
They sacrificed the Ark immigrant
group for their own survival?

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.470
Hang on. What about the Others?

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:57.560
The moon's government created the belt,
but what of the Others that fall from it?

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:01.310
The Moon has a space station
outside the belt.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:05.400
It releases the genetic information
of living organisms.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:11.450
When it encounters the Other Particles,
Others are spawned,

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.870
and they rain down to earth.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.160
They'd really go that far?

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.920
Our records say the Moon
was overpopulated back then.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:26.800
So it may have also been
a means of population control.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.380
Even so...!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:33.010
That probably means the Moon folk,
too, were struggling to survive.

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:36.930
Long story short, I had no choice
but to stay on earth.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:40.350
I've no idea what happened
on the Moon after that.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:44.440
I don't even know if
humankind still exists there.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:48.980
Even if they did survive,
many have likely turned into Others.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:54.200
Kasane.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:58.410
Can you forgive the moon people
after what they did to you?

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:04.960
I understand why you might think
like that, but it's ancient history.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:06.540
And here we are.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.420
Looks like everyone's here.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:24.690
This leads to the foot of the mountain.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.810
Our armored vehicle's down there.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.480
You said we're taking
a risk by going this way.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:35.570
Yeah, but if our luck holds out...

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:38.580
What's that?!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.200
Our luck just ran out.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:48.380
Something moving underground!
And it's really big!

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:12.820
I still can't believe
I lost Alice like that.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:15.450
You haven't lost her yet.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.610
That I promise you.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:40.350
How about this?!

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.020
No way.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:50.190
What's with this thing? Nothing works?

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:51.820
Let's fall back for now.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.360
I agree.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:03.910
It's an Other that's long
made this place its home.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:09.670
We've battled it many times
but were never able to defeat it.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.920
That explains why the area is off-limits.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:17.670
We're just lucky that it
never comes this far.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.390
Is there any way to get around it?

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:24.600
The beast lies along the only route
to the base of the mountain.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.600
Could we run past it?

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.940
It's unexpectedly fast.

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:33.360
Plus, its icicle attack covers
a pretty wide area.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.860
What if we used Luka's power?

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.280
We don't know where it will surface.

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:40.610
That makes teleportation risky.

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:46.120
Yeah, you never know where it might be.
This cavern is like a maze.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.330
Suoh is closing in.

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:53.920
Then our only choice
is to fight that Other.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:57.210
I'll see if I can find another way out.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.760
I don't think you'll have much luck.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:05.720
He's right. There are many branches,
twists, and turns, just like a maze.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.600
Told you so.

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:08.600
What is it?

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.600
I found a really large area.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:13.980
But it's strange.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.610
Strange?

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.950
There's a big hollow area below it.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.320
How thick is the ground?

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.200
It's not that thick.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:31.790
Hanabi, Gemma, Shiden,
Luka, Tsugumi. Stand by here.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:37.880
Yuito, Kasane, Kagero, Arashi,
and I will lure the creature here.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.760
Sounds like a plan. Let's do it.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:46.930
Kagero.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:48.350
Yeah?

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:52.060
If that story about you
emigrating from the moon is true,

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.520
why are you helping us?

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:59.900
It's not that simple.
I have my own reason for helping you.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:04.740
The Moon abandoned us on earth,
so we founded our own nation.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:07.160
That would be New Himuka.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.200
And Yakumo Sumeragi was our founder.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.250
But you've already heard this.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.710
Yeah.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:18.300
However, some never gave up
on returning to the Moon.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:23.840
They were the ones who founded Togetsu,
and I was among them.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.430
We entered cold sleep,

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:30.560
and took turns waking to assess
the situation here on earth

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.310
and to try contacting the Moon.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:38.320
After several rounds of this, I woke
to find that Togetsu had changed.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:42.360
There was no returning to the Moon
while the Extinction Belt remained.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:48.410
Not only that, we didn't know how
the Moon had fared against the Others.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.200
So we hatched a plan.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:54.710
To save our motherland, the Moon,
and escape from earth,

00:14:54.710 --> 00:15:00.090
we would make it so that the Ark
immigrant project never existed.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:05.260
The Red Strings... The power
to travel through time.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:10.220
So you want to turn back time
so that none of that ever happened.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:15.310
To right this universe gone wrong
and forge the future as it should be,

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.560
that is Togetsu's objective.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.110
And we're to believe such a crazy story?

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:22.650
Whether or not you believe it,

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:28.570
Togetsu has created the Red Strings
to make it happen.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:34.450
But why Yuito has the exact same
power is a complete mystery.

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:36.870
Yuito, Kasane.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.210
We're ready over here.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.720
The Suoh forces are
approaching the cavern.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:49.220
We better hurry. Commence the operation.

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:21.080
That's enough! Let's go!

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:27.590
Here it comes!

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:40.350
Yuito!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.900
It's nothing!

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:51.320
So Kagero's story is all true?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.330
Yes, every word of it.

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:58.000
Then this is no time for petty squabbles
between Suoh and Seiran.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:02.960
It will be like we never existed
if Togetsu achieves its designs.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:06.550
That can't happen!
I won't be written out of existence!

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:10.510
We're all here fighting for our lives,
and that means something!

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:15.390
There's a branch up ahead. Take a right.

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:17.270
Just 500 meters more.

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:20.770
...300, 200, 100...

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:22.310
Here it comes!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.440
Now!

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.180
It'll take one more!

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:56.390
Just a little more.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:02.310
Tsugumi, run!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.730
No, it's now or never.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:19.490
She did it!

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.870
Perhaps, we've both lived too long.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.920
Rest in peace down there.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.170
Everyone okay?!

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.260
Yeah.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.220
What a relief.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.510
No hostiles nearby.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.140
Wataru, let us know
if anything else happens.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.350
You can count on me.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.850
You, too, Haruka.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.480
Say no more!

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:49.480
Kagero.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.530
You never finished your story.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.200
So let's hear it.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.490
Why did you say you have your own reason?

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:03.080
I was spying for Togetsu.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:06.960
I was their mole in Suoh,
delivering them intel.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:09.630
So why is their spy helping us?

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:13.970
At first, it was to thwart Togetsu's plan.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:16.090
I pretended to follow orders

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.510
so they wouldn't uncover my betrayal.

00:19:21.850 --> 00:19:24.940
Time to fall back, don't you think?

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:29.150
That's a convenient story.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:32.570
If you don't like it,
we can part ways right here.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:37.240
But I won't let this world's history
be erased.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:40.160
I left a family back on the Moon.

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:47.500
They will <i>not </i>wipe
my child from existence!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.880
Kagero's serious.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:56.340
I can tell. I haven't seen him
like this in a long time.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:59.340
You have to believe him.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.430
Tsugumi.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:05.560
Tsugumi knows you best,
so if she says so, I believe you.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:08.440
Me, too. I believe you, Kagero.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:11.230
But betray us, and we'll kill you.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.780
This is classic.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:19.160
I had taken you guys for a bunch of noobs.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:23.950
What are we gonna do now?

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:27.330
We thwart Togetsu's plan.
That's all we can do.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:31.960
But that sounds like biting off
way more than I can chew.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.010
What if we appeal to the leaders
of Suoh and Seiran?

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:37.220
We're currently outlaws.

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:40.090
But once they hear about Togetsu's plan,

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:43.930
I bet they'll realize this is no time
to be fighting each other.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.520
I wonder.

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:50.650
The governments of Suoh and Seiran should
know all about the Moon's ARK mission.

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:53.980
So it appears they're acting
in their own interests.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.900
Even so, we have to do something.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:01.320
None of us wants to be
erased from existence.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.910
That's true.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:05.870
Let's split up and do what we can.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:11.370
Kasane?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.460
Okay, I'm coming.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:20.220
Yuito, I need to say this again.
I'm sorry for trying to kill you.

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:25.640
But I wasn't the one who killed
your father, Chairman Sumeragi.

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:27.680
Yeah, I know.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.560
I remembered something
after fighting beside you again.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:35.020
You're a terrible liar, Kasane.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.690
What?! Are you making fun of me?

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:44.280
I'll try to persuade the top
leaders in Suoh.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:47.740
This time, my brother and I
need to have a good talk.

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:50.330
I'll go to Seiran.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:53.000
We finally want the same thing.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:56.090
Yes. Good luck.

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.100
Yuito.

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:17.900
Yuito.

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:19.820
Yuito.

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:23.570
Yuito.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:26.740
Yuito...

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:11.930
Nagi Attacks
